{"version":1,"slug":"organized__Others__Quantitative_Aptitude__General_Quant__SSC_CGL_MOCKS_2025_SSC_SUPER_PRACTICE_41941","path":"organized/Others/Quantitative Aptitude/General Quant/@SSC_CGL_MOCKS_2025_SSC SUPER PRACTICE_41941.html","title":"devgagan","provider":"organized","category":"Others/Quantitative Aptitude/General Quant","durationMinutes":60,"totalQuestions":20,"sectionsLocked":false,"sections":null,"questions":[{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Sum of two numbers is 381 and difference between them is 135. Find the larger number.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; 381 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; 135 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">324</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">324</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">278</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">278</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">258</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">258</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">345</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">345</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Let the numbers be a and b</p><p>a + b = 381..........(i)</p><p>a  -  b = 135.........(ii)</p><p>from (ii) </p><p>a = 135 + b</p><p>Putting value of a in (i) we get,</p><p>135 + b + b = 381</p><p>2b = 246</p><p>b = 123</p><p>a = 135 + 123 = 258</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>After two years, Pallavi's age was 3 times of Firoz's age. The ratio between Firoz's age 4 years hence and Pallavi's age 5 years hence, will be 4: 11 respectively. If Bhim is 6 years older than Firoz, then what was Bhim's age five years ago?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2366;&#2354; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342;, &#2346;&#2354;&#2381;&#2354;&#2357;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2313;&#2350;&#2381;&#2352; &#2347;&#2367;&#2352;&#2379;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2313;&#2350;&#2381;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2341;&#2368;&#2404; 4 &#2360;&#2366;&#2354; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2347;&#2367;&#2352;&#2379;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2313;&#2350;&#2381;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; 5 &#2360;&#2366;&#2354; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2346;&#2354;&#2381;&#2354;&#2357;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2313;&#2350;&#2381;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 4:11 &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2349;&#2368;&#2350; &#2347;&#2367;&#2352;&#2379;&#2332; &#2360;&#2375; 6 &#2360;&#2366;&#2354; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2346;&#2366;&#2306;&#2330; &#2360;&#2366;&#2354; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2375; &#2349;&#2368;&#2350; &#2325;&#2368; &#2313;&#2350;&#2381;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2341;&#2368;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">9 years</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">9 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">11 years</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">11 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">10 years</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">10 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">12 years</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">12 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Let present age of Pallavi and Firoz are (3x - 2) years and (x - 2) years, respectively.</p><p>(x - 2 + 4)/(3x - 2 + 5) = 4/11</p><p>=&gt; x = 10</p><p>Hence, Bhim's age five years ago = (10  -  2 + 6 - 5) = 9 years</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>How much does one need to subtract from 3/5 to obtain 4/7?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>4/7 &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; 3/5 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2328;&#2335;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">9/32</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">9/32</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">9/34</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">9/34</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1/35</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1/35</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">8/35</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">8/35</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Let the number subtracted = x</p><p>3/5  -  x = 4/7</p><p>x = 3/5  -  4/7</p><p>x = (21  -  20)/35</p><p>x = 1/35</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Ratio of present age of A to B is 3:5 and after 6 years the ratio becomes 21:31. Find the age of B before 3 years. </p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>A &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; &#2325;&#2366; B &#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 3:5 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; 6 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2351;&#2361; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 21:31 &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; 3 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2375; B &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">20 years</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">20 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">23 years</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">23 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">22 years</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">22 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">24 years</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">24 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Let the present age of A and B be 3x years and 5x years respectively.</p><p>According to question,</p><p>(3x + 6)/(5x + 6) = 21/31</p><p>93x + 186 = 105x + 126</p><p>x = 5 </p><p>Present age of B = 5 * 5 = 25 years</p><p>Age of B before 3 years = 25  -  3 = 22 years</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The digit on tens place of a two-digit number is 4/3 of the digit on ones place. When the digits are interchanged, the difference between both the numbers is 18. Find the sum of the digits of the number.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2361;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366; 4/3 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2332;&#2348; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2310;&#2346;&#2360; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2342;&#2354; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; 18 &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">14</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">14</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">18</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">18</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">15</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">15</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">11</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">11</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Let the digit on ones place = 3m</p><p>Digit on tens place = 4m</p><p>According to the question-</p><p>(10*4m + 3m)  -  (10*3m + 4m) = 18</p><p>43m  -  34m = 18</p><p>m = 2</p><p>So, the number = 86</p><p>Required sum = 8 + 6 = 14</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In a park, there are goats and hens in the ratio 7: 11. If legs are counted, the total number of legs is 500. Find the number of goats.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2325; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2325;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; &#2324;&#2352; &#2350;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; 7:11 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2346;&#2376;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2367;&#2344;&#2340;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319; &#2340;&#2379; &#2346;&#2376;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 500 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2348;&#2325;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">70</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">70</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">56</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">56</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">77</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">77</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">84</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">84</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Let the number of goats and hens be 7X and 11X respectively.</p><p>According to the question,</p><p>7X * 4 + 11X * 2 = 500</p><p>50X = 500</p><p>X = 10</p><p>Number of goats = 7X = 70</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Two chairs and one fan cost Rs.14000, while two fans and one chair cost Rs.19600. The value of one fan is:</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2325;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2360;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2306;&#2326;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; 14000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2348;&#2325;&#2367; &#2342;&#2379; &#2346;&#2306;&#2326;&#2379;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2360;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; 19600 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2306;&#2326;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;:</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Rs.7200</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;.7200</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs.8400</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;.8400</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs.10600</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;.10600</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs.6400</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;.6400</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Let the cost of one fan and one chair be Rs. X and Rs. Y respectively.</p><p>Given that,</p><p>2Y + X = 14000 ... (1)</p><p>And</p><p>2X + Y = 19600 ... (2)</p><p>Solving equations (1) and (2),</p><p>X = 8400</p><p>Value of one fan = Rs.8400</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>A zookeeper counted a total of 80 heads in an enclosure. Upon checking, he found that there were 220 legs. If the only animals present were kangaroos and parrots, where each kangaroo had four legs and each parrot had two, how many kangaroos were in the enclosure?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2330;&#2367;&#2337;&#2364;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2328;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2326;&#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2344;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; 80 &#2360;&#2367;&#2352; &#2327;&#2367;&#2344;&#2375;&#2404; &#2332;&#2366;&#2305;&#2330; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367; &#2357;&#2361;&#2366;&#2305; 220 &#2346;&#2376;&#2352; &#2341;&#2375;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2361;&#2366;&#2305; &#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; &#2325;&#2306;&#2327;&#2366;&#2352;&#2370; &#2324;&#2352; &#2340;&#2379;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2368; &#2350;&#2380;&#2332;&#2370;&#2342; &#2341;&#2375;, &#2332;&#2361;&#2366;&#2305; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2325;&#2306;&#2327;&#2366;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2375; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2346;&#2376;&#2352; &#2341;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2340;&#2379;&#2340;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2346;&#2376;&#2352; &#2341;&#2375;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2348;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2306;&#2327;&#2366;&#2352;&#2370; &#2341;&#2375;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">30</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">30</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">50</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">50</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">40</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">40</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">60</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">60</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Number of heads = number of kangaroos + number of parrots</p><p>Let number of parrots be X.</p><p>Then number of kangaroos be (80  -  X).</p><p>Total number of legs = 220</p><p>2X + 4(80  -  X) = 220</p><p>2X + 320  -  4X = 220</p><p>2X = 100</p><p>X = 50</p><p>Number of kangaroos = 80  -  50 = 30</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>At a gaming arcade, all game tokens cost the same, and there is an additional entry fee of &#8377;200. Virat played 10 games and spent a total of &#8377;1,000 during his visit. How much (in &#8377;) would Virat have to pay if he played 16 games?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2327;&#2375;&#2350;&#2367;&#2306;&#2327; &#2310;&#2352;&#2381;&#2325;&#2375;&#2337; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2327;&#2375;&#2350; &#2335;&#2379;&#2325;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2361;&#2366;&#2306; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2358;&#2369;&#2354;&#2381;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 200 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2309;&#2340;&#2367;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2367;&#2352;&#2366;&#2335; &#2344;&#2375; 10 &#2327;&#2375;&#2350; &#2326;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2351;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2380;&#2352;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; 1,000 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2326;&#2352;&#2381;&#2330; &#2325;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404; &#2309;&#2327;&#2352; &#2357;&#2367;&#2352;&#2366;&#2335; &#2344;&#2375; 16 &#2327;&#2375;&#2350; &#2326;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; (1,000 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2349;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Rs.1620</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;.1620</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs.1290</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;.1290</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs.1380</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;.1380</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs.1480</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;.1480</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Let the cost of one token be Rs. X</p><p>Given that,</p><p>10 games + entry fee = Rs.1000</p><p>10X + 200 = 1000</p><p>10X = 800</p><p>X = 80</p><p>If the number of games is 16, then total amount paid by Virat = 16 X 80 + 200 = 1280 + 200 = Rs.1480</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The ratio of VIP and Regular concert ticket prices for a music festival is 7:4, and the ratio of the number of VIP to Regular ticket holders is 2:5. If the total revenue collected from ticket sales on a particular day was &#8377;51000, find the amount collected from Regular ticket holders.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2327;&#2368;&#2340; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2361; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2357;&#2368;&#2310;&#2312;&#2346;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2344;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350;&#2367;&#2340; &#2360;&#2306;&#2327;&#2368;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350; &#2335;&#2367;&#2325;&#2335; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 7:4 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2368;&#2310;&#2312;&#2346;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2344;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350;&#2367;&#2340; &#2335;&#2367;&#2325;&#2335; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 2:5 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2357;&#2367;&#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344; &#2335;&#2367;&#2325;&#2335; &#2348;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368; &#2360;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2352;&#2366;&#2332;&#2360;&#2381;&#2357; &#8377;51000 &#2341;&#2366;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2344;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350;&#2367;&#2340; &#2335;&#2367;&#2325;&#2335; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Rs.30000</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;.30000</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs.40000</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;.40000</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs.25000</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">25,000</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs.20000</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;.20000</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Let the prices of VIP and Regular ticket holders be 7X and 4X respectively.</p><p>And the number of VIP to Regular ticket holders be 2Y and 5Y respectively.</p><p>Total revenue = 51000</p><p>(7X * 2Y) + (4X * 5Y) = Rs.51000</p><p>14XY + 20XY = 51000</p><p>34XY = 51000</p><p>XY = 1500</p><p>Amount collected from regular ticket holders = 4X * 5Y = 20XY = 20 * 1500 = Rs.30000</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>At a zoo, the entry fee is &#8377;100, and each visitor can purchase animal feed at a fixed price per pack. Riya bought 8 packs of animal feed and paid a total of &#8377;1,700 for her visit. How much would she have to pay if she bought 12 packs of animal feed?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2330;&#2367;&#2337;&#2364;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2328;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2358;&#2369;&#2354;&#2381;&#2325; 100 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2310;&#2327;&#2306;&#2340;&#2369;&#2325; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2346;&#2376;&#2325;&#2375;&#2335; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2358;&#2369; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2358;&#2369; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; 8 &#2346;&#2376;&#2325;&#2375;&#2335; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2351;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; 1,700 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2349;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2309;&#2327;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2358;&#2369; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; 12 &#2346;&#2376;&#2325;&#2375;&#2335; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2375; &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2349;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Rs.2000</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2000</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs.2400</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;.2400</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs.2800</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;.2800</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs.2500</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2500</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Let the price of each pack be Rs. X.</p><p>Given that,</p><p>8X + 100 = Rs.1700</p><p>8X = 1600</p><p>X = 200</p><p>Total amount paid if she bought 12 packs of animal feed = 12 x 200 + 100 = Rs.2500</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>At a bookstore, Meera bought notebooks for her 6 classmates for a total of &#8377;280. Some of them wanted ruled notebooks, while others preferred plain notebooks. A ruled notebook costs &#8377;40, and a plain notebook costs &#8377;50. How many plain notebooks did she purchase?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2366;&#2348; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344; &#2346;&#2352; &#2350;&#2368;&#2352;&#2366; &#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; 6 &#2360;&#2361;&#2346;&#2366;&#2336;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#8377;280 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2344;&#2379;&#2335;&#2348;&#2369;&#2325; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2368;&#2404; &#2313;&#2344;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2369;&#2331; &#2344;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2337; &#2344;&#2379;&#2335;&#2348;&#2369;&#2325; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2368;, &#2332;&#2348;&#2325;&#2367; &#2309;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351; &#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2354;&#2375;&#2344; &#2344;&#2379;&#2335;&#2348;&#2369;&#2325; &#2346;&#2360;&#2306;&#2342; &#2325;&#2368;&#2404; &#2352;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2337; &#2344;&#2379;&#2335;&#2348;&#2369;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#8377;40 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2354;&#2375;&#2344; &#2344;&#2379;&#2335;&#2348;&#2369;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#8377;50 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2354;&#2375;&#2344; &#2344;&#2379;&#2335;&#2348;&#2369;&#2325; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2368;&#2306;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">3</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">2</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">4</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Let number of plain notebooks bought be X then number of ruled notebooks be (6  -  X).</p><p>Given that,</p><p>50X + 40(6  -  X) = 280</p><p>50X + 240  -  40X = 280</p><p>X = 4</p><p>The number of plain notebooks bought is 4.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>A school sports teacher purchases 7 badminton rackets and 6 shuttlecocks for &#8377;7600. Later, she buys 3 badminton rackets and 5 shuttlecocks for &#8377;3500. Find the cost of each racket and each shuttlecock respectively.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2379;&#2352;&#2381;&#2335;&#2381;&#2360; &#2335;&#2368;&#2330;&#2352; &#2344;&#2375; 7 &#2348;&#2376;&#2337;&#2350;&#2367;&#2306;&#2335;&#2344; &#2352;&#2376;&#2325;&#2375;&#2335; &#2324;&#2352; 6 &#2358;&#2335;&#2354;&#2325;&#2377;&#2325; 7600 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2375;&#2404; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; 3 &#2348;&#2376;&#2337;&#2350;&#2367;&#2306;&#2335;&#2344; &#2352;&#2376;&#2325;&#2375;&#2335; &#2324;&#2352; 5 &#2358;&#2335;&#2354;&#2325;&#2377;&#2325; 3500 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2375;&#2404; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2352;&#2376;&#2325;&#2375;&#2335; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2358;&#2335;&#2354;&#2325;&#2377;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Rs.500 and Rs.50</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">500 &#2352;&#2369;. &#2324;&#2352; 50 &#2352;&#2369;.</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs.1000 and Rs.100</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1000 &#2352;&#2369;. &#2324;&#2352; 100 &#2352;&#2369;.</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs.500 and Rs.100</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">500 &#2352;&#2369;. &#2324;&#2352; 100 &#2352;&#2369;.</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs.1000 and Rs.150</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1000 &#2352;&#2369;. &#2324;&#2352; 150 &#2352;&#2369;.</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Let price of each racket and each shuttlecock be Rs. A, and Rs. B respectively.</p><p>Given that,</p><p>7A + 6B = 7600 ... (1)</p><p>3A + 5B = 3500 ... (2)</p><p>After solving equation (1) and (2).</p><p>B = 100 and A = 1000</p><p>Therefore,</p><p>Cost of each racket = Rs.1000</p><p>And cost of each shuttlecock = Rs.100</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Let there are two numbers A and B such that difference between them is 52 and A = B/3. Find the value of A.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2354;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2325;&#2367; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; 52 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; A = B/3 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; A &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">13</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">13</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">26</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">26</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">39</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">39</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">24</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">24</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Given B = 3A</p><p>Also given B  -  A = 52</p><p>3A  -  A = 52</p><p>A = 26</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The cost of 4 desks and 2 stools together is &#8377;3200, while the cost of 2 desks and 5 stools together is &#8377;2800. Find the total cost of 1 desk and 4 stools.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>4 &#2337;&#2375;&#2360;&#2381;&#2325; &#2324;&#2352; 2 &#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2370;&#2354; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#8377;3200 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2348;&#2325;&#2367; 2 &#2337;&#2375;&#2360;&#2381;&#2325; &#2324;&#2352; 5 &#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2370;&#2354; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#8377;2800 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; 1 &#2337;&#2375;&#2360;&#2381;&#2325; &#2324;&#2352; 4 &#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2370;&#2354; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Rs.1650</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;.1650</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs.2100</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;.2100</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs.1850</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;.1850</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs.1900</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;.1900</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Let the cost of 1 desk and 1 stool be Rs. A, and Rs. B respectively.</p><p>Given that</p><p>4A + 2B = 3200</p><p>2A + B = 1600 ... (1)</p><p>And</p><p>2A + 5B = 2800 ... (2)</p><p>After solving equations (1) and (2),</p><p>B = 300 and A = 650</p><p>Total cost of 1 desk and 4 stools = 650 + 4 * 300 = 650 + 1200 = Rs.1850</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>A fraction becomes 3/4 if 1 is added to both its numerator and denominator. However, if 4 is subtracted from each, the fraction becomes 2/5. Find the fraction.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2358; &#2324;&#2352; &#2361;&#2352; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 1 &#2332;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319; &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2361; 3/4 &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2361;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366;&#2305;&#2325;&#2367;, &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 4 &#2328;&#2335;&#2366; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319; &#2340;&#2379; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; 2/5 &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">38/53</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">38/53</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">19/53</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">19/53</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">38/51</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">38/51</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">19/51</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">19/51</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Let the fraction be A/B.</p><p>Given</p><p>(A + 1)/ (B + 1) = 3/4</p><p>4A + 4 = 3B + 3</p><p>3B  -  4A = 1 ... (1)</p><p>And</p><p>(A  -  4)/ (B  -  4) = 2/5</p><p>5A  -  20 = 2B  -  8</p><p>5A  -  2B = 12 ... (2)</p><p>5A = 12 + 2B</p><p>A = (12 + 2B)/5</p><p>Substitute the value in equation 1,</p><p>3B  -  [(48 + 8B)/5] = 1</p><p>15B  -  48  -  8B = 5</p><p>7B = 53</p><p>B = 53/7</p><p>Now,</p><p>A = [12 + (106/7)]/5</p><p>A = 190/35</p><p>A = 38/7</p><p>Fraction = (38/7)/ (53/7) = 38/53</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Emma and Jack each have a collection of pencils. If Emma gives one pencil to Jack, they will both have an equal number of pencils. Conversely, if Jack gives one pencil to Emma, she will end up with three times the number of pencils that Jack has. What is the total number of pencils they both have?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2350;&#2381;&#2350;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2332;&#2376;&#2325; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360; &#2346;&#2375;&#2306;&#2360;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2361; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2309;&#2327;&#2352; &#2319;&#2350;&#2381;&#2350;&#2366; &#2332;&#2376;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2375;&#2306;&#2360;&#2367;&#2354; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2344; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2375;&#2306;&#2360;&#2367;&#2354;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2379;&#2306;&#2327;&#2368;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2340;, &#2309;&#2327;&#2352; &#2332;&#2376;&#2325; &#2319;&#2350;&#2381;&#2350;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2375;&#2306;&#2360;&#2367;&#2354; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360; &#2332;&#2376;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360; &#2350;&#2380;&#2332;&#2370;&#2342; &#2346;&#2375;&#2306;&#2360;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2375; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2346;&#2375;&#2306;&#2360;&#2367;&#2354;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2379;&#2306;&#2327;&#2368;&#2404; &#2313;&#2344; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2346;&#2375;&#2306;&#2360;&#2367;&#2354;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">6</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">6</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">10</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">10</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">8</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">8</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">12</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">12</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Let the number of pencils Emma has be X, and the number of pencils jack has be Y.</p><p>Given that</p><p>X  -  1 = Y + 1</p><p>X  -  Y = 2 ... (1)</p><p>And</p><p>(X + 1) = 3(Y  -  1)</p><p>X + 1 = 3Y  -  3</p><p>X  -  3Y = -4</p><p>3Y  -  X = 4 ... (2)</p><p>After solving equations (1) and (2),</p><p>Y = 3 and X = 5</p><p>Total number of pencils Emma and Jack have is 8.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>A farm has some turkeys and sheep. If the total number of heads is 50 and the total number of legs is 134, how many turkeys are there on the farm?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2347;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2369;&#2331; &#2335;&#2352;&#2381;&#2325;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2349;&#2375;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2367;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 50 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2376;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 134 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2347;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2335;&#2352;&#2381;&#2325;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">31</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">31</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">29</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">29</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">33</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">33</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">32</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">32</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Let number of turkeys be X then number of sheep are (50  -  X).</p><p>Total number of legs = 134</p><p>2X + 4(50  -  X) = 134</p><p>2X + 200  -  4X = 134</p><p>2X = 66</p><p>X = 33</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The cost of 30 books and 15 pens is Rs.1050. Find the cost of 2 books and 1 pen.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>30 &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2366;&#2348;&#2379;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; 15 &#2325;&#2354;&#2350;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; 1050 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; 2 &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2366;&#2348;&#2379;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; 1 &#2325;&#2354;&#2350; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Rs.70</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">70</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs.60</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">60</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs.40</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">40</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs.80</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">80</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Given that</p><p>30 books + 15 pens = Rs.1050</p><p>15(2 books + 1 pen) = Rs.1050</p><p>2 books + 1 pen = Rs.70</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Two number X and Y are such that Y  -  X = 12 and Y: X = 3: 1. Find the value of X + 3Y.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; X &#2324;&#2352; Y &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367; Y - X = 12 &#2324;&#2352; Y: X = 3: 1 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; X + 3Y &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">50</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">50</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">64</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">64</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">72</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">72</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">60</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">60</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Let Y = 3A and X = A.</p><p>Given Y  -  X = 12</p><p>3A  -  A = 12</p><p>2A = 12</p><p>A = 6</p><p>So, Y = 18 and X = 6</p><p>Therefore,</p><p>X + 3Y = 6 + 54 = 60</p>","marks":2,"section":null}]}